  "items": [
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "The Ukrainian government declares April 6 as a day of mourning following yesterday's Russian missile strike on Kryvyi Rih in Dnipropetrovsk Oblast, Ukraine, that killed nineteen people, one of the deadliest strikes since the start of the invasion. ((de Volkskrant))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Colonel Nur Farey, the senior Somali military commander of the 14th brigade, is assassinated by a man believed to be an al-Shabaab militant in Addow Dibille near Afgoye, Lower Shabelle, Somalia. ((Hiiraan Online))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Business and economy",
      "text": "The first of two tariff rounds go into effect in the United States, containing a 10% blanket tariff on every import into the country. The second round of country-specific tariffs is scheduled to go into effect on April 9. ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "International relations",
      "text": "Israel blocks two UK MPs from entering the country. ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Politics and elections",
      "text": "\"Hands Off\" protests against U.S. President Donald Trump occur throughout the country. ((The New York Times))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Sports",
      "text": "Nick Rockett, rode by Irish jockey Patrick Mullins, wins the 2025 Grand National horse race at Aintree Racecourse in England. ((BBC Sport))"
    },
